      "writtenOn": "2022-06-20T02:33:32Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure this is a great choice of test to run on automotive; unit tests shouldn\u0027t be very important since as long as the code was not modified, and you\u0027d probably want CTS tests instead to check the overall behavior. If the code is modified in an auto branch, I think the tests should also only be marked as automotive-tests in that branch. There\u0027s some cost on our side to maintain the build rules/tests for the automotive-tests target, so we should make sure that what is included is really what we need.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 13,
        "startChar": 48,
        "endLine": 13,
        "endChar": 61
      },
      "revId": "4fe6b7455800ace8db90e025ca1995615f464011",
